## Key Concepts
- Three-valued Kleene logic with a custom ⊕ priority-merge operator
- Forward-checking and constraint propagation under non-classical connectives
- Constraint satisfaction with minimal assumptions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch of propagation loop using given semantics
function propagate(constraints, domains) {
  while (changes) {
    changes = false;
    for (const constraint of constraints) {
      for (const assignment of domains) {
        const result = evaluate(constraint, assignment);
        if (result === 'F') {
          domains = prune(domains, assignment);
          changes = true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return domains;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests reasoning with temporal and tri-valued logic, combining forward propagation with unknowns and discrete time.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued semantics
- Temporal horizons and propagation
- Backtracking with partial assignments

## Code Example
```javascript
function check(trace){
  for(let t=0;t<3;t++){
    if(trace.X1[t]==="T" && trace.X2[t+1]==="F") return false;
    if(trace.X2[t]==="F" && trace.X3[t+1]!=="T") return false;
    if(trace.X3[t]==="U" && trace.X1[t+2]!=="U") return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

